---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { company } from "../data/company";
import { areas } from "../data/areas";
import CallStrip from "../components/CallStrip.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Areas We Cover | LeonEast Roofing & Building"
  description="LeonEast Roofing covers Bromley, Beckenham, Chislehurst, Petts Wood, Orpington, Sidcup, Swanley and the towns between. No travel charge anywhere on the list."
>
  <section class="bg-carbon text-white">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 sm:px-6 py-12">
      <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-bold leading-tight">Areas we cover</h1>
      <p class="mt-5 max-w-3xl text-lg text-mist">
        We work out of Bromley, so most of the BR postcodes are ten to twenty minutes away.
        There is no travel charge on anywhere in this list.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 sm:px-6 py-14">
    <ul class="grid gap-x-8 gap-y-3 sm:grid-cols-3">
      {areas.map((a) => (
        <li class="border-b border-graphite/10 py-2 font-semibold text-carbon">{a}</li>
      ))}
    </ul>

    <div class="mt-12 grid lg:grid-cols-2 gap-10 items-start">
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-carbon">A note on the boundaries</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-graphite/80">
          Two of these are not in Bromley and it catches people out when they need planning
          advice. Sidcup is the London Borough of Bexley. Swanley has a BR postcode but is
          not in London at all - it is Sevenoaks District Council, in Kent. Biggin Hill goes
          the other way: a TN postcode and thoroughly Kentish, but Bromley for planning.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-graphite/80">
          For a repair none of that matters, because like-for-like maintenance needs no
          permission anywhere. It only comes up if you are changing the shape or the look of
          the roof.
        </p>
        <h2 class="mt-8 text-2xl font-bold text-carbon">Not on the list?</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-graphite/80">
          Ring and ask. If you are just outside we will usually still come, and if you are
          far enough out that somebody closer would serve you better, we will say so rather
          than quote you a travel charge.
        </p>
        <a href={company.phoneLink} class="mt-5 inline-flex rounded bg-volt px-6 py-3 font-bold text-white hover:bg-volt-deep">
          {company.phone}
        </a>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-lg overflow-hidden border border-graphite/15">
        <iframe src="https://maps.google.com/maps?q=Bromley%2C%20London&output=embed"
          width="100%" height="380" style="border:0" loading="lazy"
          referrerpolicy="no-referrer-when-downgrade" title="Map of Bromley and the surrounding area"></iframe>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CallStrip />
</Layout>
